{
  "id": "default",
  "notes": [
    "One entry per obstacle kind a recipe or generator may name. role decides the rules (low: blocks movement, not sight, Low cover; high: blocks both, High cover). silhouette decides the placeholder shape until a scene is authored: slab (wall piece aligned to its neighbours), pillar (round column), mass (hex prism), scene (load `scene`, else mass). material groups kinds that can share a sculpted mesh with a material swap.",
    "Recipes normally name a ROLE (low, high, pillar) and let their obstacles palette pick the kind. Name a kind directly only when the layout is about that specific thing (the courtyard ring is a wall)."
